          "heading": "Henry Slade opens up on managing diabetes during his England career",
          "body": "England centre Henry Slade has spoken openly about the reality of managing Type one diabetes throughout his professional career. Diagnosed at 18, the Exeter Chiefs midfielder admitted the diagnosis was a 'tough pill to swallow' but was inspired by his father, John, who also has the condition. Slade, now a key figure in Steve Borthwick's national set-up, revealed he never doubted his ability to play rugby at the highest level despite the daily challenges of regulating his blood sugar."
