          "kicker": "Women's Test",
          "heading": "Ireland women cruise past Japan in Cork for second consecutive victory",
          "body": "The Ireland women's national team overcame an early deficit to beat Japan 43-19 at Virgin Media Park in Cork. After conceding a rolling-maul try in the opening minutes, the hosts utilised their superior scrum dominance to win penalties and territory. Flyhalf Dannah O'Brien's tactical kicking constantly troubled the visitors' back field, while Aoife Dalton gained crucial metres with every carry. The victory completes a back-to-back double over the visitors, following a 31-24 win in Galway."
